  "conclusion": "No all-linear group size passed every numerical gate. The group-8 four-family search found seven passing selective masks; the best was o_proj plus gate/up, estimating 898,498,560 deployed weight bytes, 12.059 whole-model bits per parameter, and a 24.629% reduction from the unique BF16 logical baseline. That selected mask subsequently passed the same five gates against a BF16 baseline over 4,096 contiguous held-out WikiText-2 targets. This strengthens the teacher-forced model-specific selectivity evidence, but runtime weights remained uncompressed and packed-kernel correctness, throughput, latency, energy, task success, serving cost, and dollars per token remain unmeasured."
